WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.300
Three hard messages: a cold email, an interruption, a disagreement.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:09.050
First, the cold email. Bagas writes to an alumna he has never met.

3
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:17.760
His first draft talks about himself, and asks for sometime. The second draft shows his homework in line one. The first line has one job: to earn the second line.

4
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:25.940
And the ask is small, specific and time-boxed.

5
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:31.810
Second, the interruption. Bagas is thirty seconds into his update when his lead cuts in: wait, what is the bottom line?

6
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:38.590
It is not an attack. It is a request for a different altitude. He answers in one sentence, then asks: shall I go into the detail?

7
00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:47.240
Third, disagreeing upward. His lead wants to spend the whole budget on one channel. Bagas thinks: that plan is wrong. Said aloud, that sentence defends his ego, not the decision.

8
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:55.600
So he shares the data, names an option, and asks a real question: what am I missing?

9
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.260
Put the three side by side. Each one starts from the other person, not from you.

10
00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:09.660
The first line must earn the second. Disagree to protect the decision, not your ego.

11
00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:14.460
Now it is your turn. Draft your own version of each message before you open the debriefs below.
